WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.540
- Well, thank you. So
nice to meet you, finally!

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.930
- Oh, finally? Okay, I'll take it.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.526
So, I know you know Salma, right?

00:00:07.526 --> 00:00:09.474
- Of course, yeah, yes.
(Salma kissing)

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:11.167
- (giggles) I was asking Salma, I'm like,

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.440
"Sometimes, when y'all
are in movies together,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.700
you don't have scenes together,"

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.757
so I was like,

00:00:15.757 --> 00:00:18.530
"Well," I was like, "Did y'all
meet?" And you did. (laughs)

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:19.363
- Yeah, but we had

00:00:19.363 --> 00:00:20.680
a lot of fun together.
- Oh, yes.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.720
- I love it, I'm so
excited about this film.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.473
So, who was the most fun on set?

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.890
- I am sitting right next to her.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.690
- Oh. (laughs)
- I have to say,

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:31.730
(audience clapping)
just so you know,

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.237
her middle name is P for party.

00:00:34.237 --> 00:00:35.890
Party girl!
- Yes.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.330
- She actually hosted this fab
Christmas party for everyone.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.830
She actually cooked for everybody.

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:43.673
- You did? For everybody?

00:00:43.673 --> 00:00:44.950
(audience cheering)
Usually people hire that out.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.640
- And there's a lot of eternals huh?

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.473
It's a lot of people.

00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:50.220
- [Kelly] That's what
I'm saying, that's a lot.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.520
- But it was homey, we
made like a real Christmas.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.390
Homey with friends and
relaxed and tequila.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.471
(audience laughing)
- Okay,

00:00:57.471 --> 00:00:58.304
I'll give you my number,

00:00:58.304 --> 00:01:00.557
I like tequila food and fun.
- She likes the tequila.

00:01:00.557 --> 00:01:02.760
- "Eternals," it's full of representation,

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.170
and we were talking about
that earlier. It's so cool.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.530
So how did you feel about representation

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.480
in film and TV whenever you were a kid?

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.450
- Well, I have to say,
growing up as a little kid,

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.160
I really didn't see a lot of
myself on TV or the big screen,

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.780
it was more like just bits
and pieces here and there.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.830
And I saw a deaf woman on
"Sesame Street," Linda Bove,

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.690
Linda the librarian, right?
(audience clapping)

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.230
I saw her and she was like me,

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:33.260
but another woman who really
inspired me was Frida Kahlo

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:39.230
and my mom at the time was a
grad student in art education

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:41.730
and she focused on Frida

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:46.010
and I just remember seeing this
beautiful, strong, talented,

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:49.300
Mexican woman who just claimed her space

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:53.375
in a world that was not ready
for a Mexican female artist.

00:01:53.375 --> 00:01:56.294
And so it really inspired me.
(audience clapping)

00:01:56.294 --> 00:01:57.334
- That's so cool.

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.430
Was that really important to
you when you played Frida?

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.263
- Yes.

00:02:00.263 --> 00:02:04.210
I think we're similar in the fact that

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:07.050
what inspired me was her
courage to be unique,

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:10.330
which is very similar
to what she's saying.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.760
And I think it's lovely that that woman,

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.773
that is no longer with us, in person,

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:19.270
inspired two girls, very
different, separately,

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:22.073
although, let me tell
you, she's half Mexican.

00:02:22.073 --> 00:02:23.893
(Kelly laughing)
- That is right.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.340
You really inspired me also

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:32.970
because this beautiful Mexican
woman who's also Lebanese

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.200
and half Mexican.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.720
So I really looked to her and
how she actually represented

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.910
and revealed her identity
and her differences

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.820
and her different intersections.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:46.900
- And the interesting thing,
(audience clapping)

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.557
while we were shooting, she
was a huge inspiration to me.

00:02:50.557 --> 00:02:52.444
- Oh, that's so cool.
I love being inspired

00:02:52.444 --> 00:02:53.363
by people I work with.
(audience clapping)

00:02:53.363 --> 00:02:55.550
- I will take that with me forever.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:59.203
- Yeah, so how did you find
out that you got the role?

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.273
- Well,

00:03:02.273 --> 00:03:03.730
I remember it was Valentine's day

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:08.351
and I was driving actually to
get some pizza for my boys,

00:03:08.351 --> 00:03:12.820
and then I got an email
and that's how I found out

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:16.420
I had to pull over and
I couldn't believe it.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.230
I was gonna be a superhero.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.970
- So cool.
- Me.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:23.840
And waiting for somebody
to jump in and say, "Psych!

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:24.673
Just kidding."

00:03:24.673 --> 00:03:28.550
- (laughs) Psych? (laughs)

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:30.560
So Lauren, could you tell
us about your character

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.910
in "Eternals?"

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:36.800
- Well, Makkari, you may
already know she's a speedster,

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.610
she's really fast, she's
traveled all over the world,

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.560
I don't even know how many times.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:45.520
And she loves art, she
loves books and really,

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.433
she just loves those earth people.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:51.180
- So do all of them not love earth people?

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.260
Is that what you're getting at? (laughs)

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.540
When she said, "Mmm."

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.700
- Some more than others.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.570
- Some more than others. (laughs)

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.870
That's a day that ends
in, "Why?" In my world.

